  "claim_contract": {
    "proved": "Finite-lattice Clifford shifts, phase-frame embeddings, and arbitrary half-link defects are packaged as continuous linear operators.  The full factorwise seven-factor straight-refinement defect is bounded by the sum of five actual spatial operator defects. Exact ordered edge reconstruction annihilates that defect independently of plaquette curvature.  A separate cubical gluing stage is controlled by a five-face curvature budget, and the composed two-stage defect is bounded by the sum of the edge and curvature budgets. Separate summability of the two scale-dependent budgets yields a single global limit and an explicit tail estimate.",
    "not_proved": "No scalar sup-norm estimate reducing each straight operator defect to max |E_i-1| is established.  No mesh-scale decay law or concrete summability of the physical Clifford walk is proved.  No continuum Dirac convergence, dynamical gauge field equation, gravity, cosmology, or empirical claim is established."
  },
